N local activation over item-field history with action values and four separate heads; field/task adaptation, not exact original DIN reproduction\",\n  \"research_goal\": \"Explore and validate mechanism-distinct unified modeling of multi-field user/context/target features and multi-feedback behavior histories. Develop representations and information flow that jointly support sequence modeling, feature interaction and task prediction under the fixed data and compute protocol.\",\n  \"architecture_search\": {\n    \"scope\": \"Whole-model design, including replacement of the initial network and all internal representations.\",\n    \"design_dimensions\": [\n      \"Representation units: fields, events, behavior groups, learned slots and target/task tokens.\",\n      \"Information flow: stacked interaction, layer-wise joint interaction, parallel exchange, learned routing or other testable unified structures.\",\n      \"History selection/compression jointly designed with target/context-conditioned retrieval.\",\n      \"Derived features computed from authorized inputs: field matches, behavior counts/composition, grouping and sequence positions.\",\n      \"Shared and task-conditioned representations, prediction readouts and registered training-loss mechanisms.\"\n    ],\n    \"lineage\": \"parent_trial identifies a comparison and evidence lineage; it does not require code or architectural inheritance. inherited_components may be empty when the whole model is replaced.\",\n    \"proposal_unit\": \"A coherent mechanism hypothesis can require several coordinated structural changes. Build that structure and plan component, replacement or factorial controls to identify where its value comes from.\",\n    \"evidence\": \"Evaluate predictive quality, mechanism support, nearest-work differences and measured cost. Compare new unified candidates against their closest architectural alternatives as well as the initial reference.\",\n    \"fixed_contracts\": \"Available sample information, labels, data split, scoring, resource accounting and the frozen host training recipe remain shared. Internal architecture and readout design are candidate choices.\",\n    \"reference_use\": \"UniRank comparison methods provide inspectable design references and nearest work. Agents choose and adapt mechanisms from local evidence.\"\n  },\n  \"research_budget\": {\n    \"seconds\": 172800,\n    \"start_event\": \"dataset_download_and_checksum_verification_completed\",\n    \"start_unix\": 1793959348.3455288,\n    \"deadline_unix\": 1794132148.3455288\n  },\n  \"test_policy\": \"closed during research; any final suite must be frozen before held-out scoring\",\n  \"source_sha256\": {\n    \"baseline.py\": \"f4b473cbacf60d72cff90f3721ad754dd617ee6065fe3fca2fc9cd4be2b25c36\",\n    \"train.py\": \"e81bdefa140a4d78cae12f4123cc421611109c84da1b9f067e23d11b6c3d335a\",\n    \"visibility.py\": \"d1f641c62fa3c72e1eadc03aad6d999cc9af87fceb783775eb22d1405d9ac6b4\",\n    \"data.py\": \"ef28cb65880b6931d3e567d2bfb4a67d7530c18067b68e47bf483b65b2560438\"\n  },\n  \"upstream_commit\": \"90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d\",\n  \"benchmark_deviations\": [\n    \"DIN is the initial empirical reference; unified research candidates can use entirely different architectures.\",\n    \"One GPU per model; batch8192 per model (single-device rather than published distributed global batch).\",\n    \"Click AUC selects models, four-task mean AUC is auxiliary.\",\n    \"Validation includes every sample; upstream default drop_last may omit remainders.\",\n    \"In-process DataLoader (num_workers=0): container shared memory is512MiB; all compared runs use the same loading policy.\",\n    \"No torch.compile; BF16; TF32 disabled.\"\n  ],\n  \"trial_cap_seconds\": 1203.3689693547785,\n  \"estimated_unit_seconds\": 481.3475877419114,\n  \"estimated_validation_seconds\": 75.22459795698524,\n  \"frozen_unix\": 1793961097.640512,\n  \"identity\": \"1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7