{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport ast,hashlib,json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nprotocol='1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7847d04fa3acf9ce71e216'\nfixed=['Frozen feature/label identity and official_offline visibility; no new inputs', 'Single-pass host training recipe, seed 20262027, split, optimizer, precision, scoring and batch size', 'Original first four residual summaries, raw match counts and 30-slot uniform/feedback compression', 'Embedding/scorer/tower modules, initialization order, five-summary adapter width16, task-specific routing and gradient ownership', 'All four fifth alternatives computed in every cell before selection; no RNG or learned modules added']\ncontrast=lambda parent,intervention,control,confounds,yes,no:dict(parent_ref=parent,intervention=intervention,control=control,held_fixed=fixed,remaining_confounds=confounds,decision_if_supported=yes,decision_if_not_supported=no)\nstudy={\n'id':'g0-r0019-coarse-cubic-replacement',\n'protocol_ref':protocol,\n'evidence_refs':['baseline-din','g2-r0004-context_only','g3-r0003-embedding_item_primary','g0-r0006-compressed_task','g0-r0009-match_detail_task','g0-r0013-block_task','g0-r0014-curvature_task','g0-r0014-duplicate_linear_task','g0-r0014-scrambled_curvature_task','g0-r0015-shared_curvature','g0-r0016-joint_ordered','g0-r0016-duplicate_match','g0-r0017-available_norm','g0-r0018-block_energy_local','g0-r0018-block_energy_reversed','g0-r0018-block_energy_global'],\n'question':'After the local gains from coarse linear and quadratic ordinal summaries, does replacing the incumbent redundant fifth match summary with a coarse cubic contrast improve full-population click AUC at fixed learned capacity, beyond a scrambled contrast and an eligibility-matched duplicate?',\n'hypothesis': 'Observed limitation: g0-r0013-block_task reaches 0.66501112 click AUC and g0-r0014-curvature_task reaches 0.66560707, above its same-capacity duplicate-linear 0.66475357 and scrambled-curvature 0.66479411 controls. These single-seed observations motivate an unresolved higher-order coarse-position signal, not a general claim that more moments help. The incumbent g0-r0017-available_norm is 0.66586052, but its fifth coefficient is just a norm-rescaled copy of the first centered target-match direction. Coarse changes orthogonal to constants, linear and quadratic block ranks are invisible to all five fixed summary coefficients (learned base compression may still observe them). A block-constant cubic residual can expose such changes without adding learned capacity. Its useful ordering information should beat both a common-gate norm-matched match duplicate and a scrambled cubic residual. Contradictory trajectories matter: direct compressed task queries g0-r0006-compressed_task scored 0.65919424 below the stronger source 0.66064694; ordered target-match-by-block interaction g0-r0016-joint_ordered scored 0.66564377 below duplicate-match 0.66573908; latest local block-energy balancing scored 0.66552831 below reversed 0.66582195 and global 0.66586052. Thus neither task conditioning, additional directions, nor locally balanced energy is uniformly beneficial. This study tests a different block-constant direction; it does not reassert those failed explanations. Baseline auxiliary AUCs (cart 0.84907, fav 0.86490, buy 0.87018) exceed incumbent auxiliary AUCs (0.78722, 0.78571, 0.78806); click gains do not establish improvement on all tasks.',\n'nearest_work':[\n {'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Archived exact-version primary text lines271-282 supports retaining unnormalized target-conditioned pooling and cautions that sequence modeling is not automatically beneficial. We retain the adapted scorer; replace one separate signed residual summary with a fixed orthogonal coarse ordinal coefficient. This is not exact DIN reproduction or an originality claim.'},\n {'source_ref':'unirank-code:UniMixer','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned benchmark forward175-200 flattens event embeddings with user/context, then learned tokenization and interaction. Here fixed masked projections retain selected sequence information before task adapters while the inherited compressed target-conditioned pooling remains. No flatten tokenizer or UniMixing blocks are adopted. Benchmark code equivalence to the original paper has not been verified.'},\n {'source_ref':'unirank-benchmark-v2','verification':'read','difference':'Cached primary benchmark section2.3 lines9,17,21,39 describes heterogeneous task tokens, flattening, sparse filtering and sequential transduction. This local comparison changes only a fixed supplemental coefficient, with none of these full architectures imported. Original-method full-paper detail is unavailable for the retrieved industry references; novelty remains unverified.'},\n {'source_ref':'trial://g0-r0017-available_norm','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Actual candidate source SHA256 2f710c8db0ad978fb51d0206205ddeb22af5c115f8ae8c624a0a7b5bc5f06f5a verified before editing. The prior fifth matches the first match direction at a different norm. The new fifth instead lies in the coarse block-constant complement of the first four directions on common support. All learned components and their allocation/initialization remain identical.'}\n],\n'inherited_components':['Full frozen host recipe and adapted DIN field/action embeddings, unnormalized local activation and four towers', 'g2 source uniform click / feedback-stratified auxiliary ten-block compression and primary-owned item/scorer gradients', 'Task-specific zero-output-initialized residual adapters; first four match/local-ordinal/coarse-linear/coarse-quadratic summaries and match counts', 'Incumbent fifth norm and availability expression retained exactly as the bridge and as the gated-duplicate basis; all existing coefficient construction retained'],\n'proposed_difference':'Replace only the fifth residual coefficient. From ten fixed block ranks r in [0,1], construct masked r\"'^3 and fixed-permutation r''^3. Two FP32 projection sweeps remove valid constants, the unscaled coarse linear coefficient and inherited fourth quadratic coefficient, with event-count weighting and recentering. Coefficients are block constant on valid events, hence also orthogonal to the centered within-block match and local-position directions in exact arithmetic. Common eligibility requires at least four occupied blocks, both new residual norm-squares >1e-10, nonzero incumbent fifth and local-position norm-squares >1e-10. Scale both new directions to the local-position coefficient norm; gated duplicate uses incumbent*eligibility and has that same norm. Bridge returns the exact incumbent coefficient ungated. All cells construct all alternatives and use the same five-channel contraction and adapters. No timestamps, sample identity, current action/labels, lookup, training change or new parameters. Rank is released array order, with no assumed elapsed-time interpretation. For exactly four occupied blocks the complement dimension is one, so ordered and scrambled residuals can be collinear; ordering attribution principally depends on histories occupying five or more blocks. Empty histories have zero residual corrections; learned shared parameters can still change their final predictions.'\"',\n'predictions':[\n 'Predeclared primary: cubic_ordered exceeds cubic_scrambled, cubic_gated_duplicate and cubic_bridge on full-population validation is_click AUC. Only improvement over both source bests and the incumbent matters for predictive progress; exceeding a weakened replacement control alone is insufficient. The incumbent comparator is 0.6658605169646938; frozen source bests are 0.660646940486458 and 0.660163362657485.',\n 'Predeclared mechanism interpretation: ordered > scrambled and eligibility-matched duplicate supports usefulness of this coarse ordering beyond summary norm, input width and eligibility. Fixed learned capacity expected32129765 total/336549 dense; host must measure it. Same-seed bridge should reproduce incumbent scores exactly under deterministic execution. It is a parity/cost bridge, not independent repeated support.',\n 'Report click logloss and all four task AUC/logloss, auxiliary mean separately, full sample/positive/negative counts, allocated GPU and wall seconds, peak memory, throughput and p50/p95 latency. Prefer no click-logloss worsening and inspect the observed auxiliary tradeoff. Same recipe isolates the coefficient; measured runtime is needed before any efficiency claim.',\n 'Use existing predeclared history bins 0,1-16,17-64,>64; negatives equal samples minus positives. History>64 is the principal exploratory ordering diagnostic, not a second selection score. Do not claim subgroup significance; new-eligibility and occupied-block diagnostics require an authorized host interface and may be unavailable. If admitted later, at least five occupied blocks is the predeclared noncollinearity diagnostic. User-cluster bootstrap and additional seeds are deferred until host resources/interfaces permit; a first-seed win remains preliminary.'\n],\n'falsifiers':[\n 'Cubic failing to exceed the incumbent bridge, or either matched replacement control, rejects useful ordered-cubic replacement for this implementation under the fixed one-pass protocol. It does not refute every higher-order history representation.',\n 'If gated duplicate improves equally, availability/gating suffices as an alternative; if scrambled is as good as ordered, new generic projection/conditioning rather than cubic order remains the explanation. A small first-seed ranking is inconclusive without repetition.',\n 'Bridge disagreement with the incumbent, changed learned parameter counts, nonfinite outputs/gradients, padded-event sensitivity, unauthorized auxiliary item/scorer gradients or failed host forward/backward/BF16 checks invalidate the comparison before performance interpretation.',\n 'If added measured runtime erases a quality-cost advantage, do not claim efficiency. If click improves but auxiliary tasks regress, report the task tradeoff instead of unified four-task superiority.'\n],\n'alternative_explanations':[\n 'Seed-specific optimization and adaptive validation selection across many earlier rounds; no held-out or repeated support exists here.',\n 'A support gate itself encodes match availability or history length; the eligibility-matched duplicate and exact bridge isolate this as far as this local comparison permits.',\n 'Normalization, coefficient distribution and optimizer conditioning remain different despite equal coefficient L2 norms and learned capacity; nonlinear adapters do not make the representations functionally equivalent.',\n 'Fixed padding/truncation and released array order can convey activity signatures rather than a causal temporal mechanism. Whole-window vocabulary and official_offline feedback assumptions remain inherited limitations.',\n 'The scrambled complement is sometimes collinear with the ordered complement, especially four-block histories, weakening the ordering contrast. BF16 coefficient quantization can also break exact algebraic orthogonality.',\n 'The common gate excludes histories with no within-block target-match contrast; this is a scoped replacement rather than a test of unconditional cubic information. Parameter learning transfers changes to ineligible histories, so slice differences cannot be attributed solely to direct access.',\n 'Primary-owned embeddings and scorer already reduce auxiliary quality relative to baseline; fixed ownership permits a click comparison but does not explain or fix that tradeoff.'\n],\n'contrasts':[\n contrast('g0-r0017-available_norm','cubic_ordered: cubic block residual','cubic_gated_duplicate: incumbent fifth under identical eligibility and coefficient norm',['Coefficient distributions and learned optimization differ; matched capacity/norm does not remove every conditioning confound.'], 'If ordered exceeds duplicate and bridge, retain as preliminary useful information replacement and schedule paired repetition.','If duplicate matches or wins, reject information-specific attribution and retain incumbent unless gating alone earns a separate controlled follow-up.'),\n contrast('g0-r0017-available_norm','cubic_ordered: true array-rank cubic after projection','cubic_scrambled: fixed [0,7,2,9,4,1,8,3,6,5] rank-permutation cube after identical projection, eligibility and norm',['Scrambled coefficient distribution differs; at four occupied blocks the residual subspace is one dimensional; no semantic recency assumption.'], 'If ordered beats scrambled and duplicate, preserve an ordering explanation as controlled single-seed support pending repetition.','If scrambled matches/wins, do not attribute gain to ordinal cubic ordering; generic extra projection/conditioning remains plausible.'),\n contrast('g0-r0017-available_norm','cubic_gated_duplicate: multiply incumbent fifth by new common eligibility','cubic_bridge: exact unmodified incumbent fifth',['Removing a channel on ineligible cases changes optimization as well as availability information.'], 'Treat a gated-duplicate gain as evidence for the gate path only; it cannot establish cubic complementarity.','If gate loses, interpret candidate versus bridge as a tradeoff between new direction and lost fifth access on sparse histories.'),\n contrast('g0-r0018-block_energy_global','cubic_bridge: incumbent return value after computing all new alternatives','g0-r0017-available_norm and g0-r0018-block_energy_global: archived same-seed incumbent expressions',['Extra unused reductions change measured compute; runtime variability; archival parity is not a repeated random seed.'], 'Require same scores under deterministic host execution and quantify shared overhead before evaluating new cells.','On mismatch diagnose numerical/operator/source differences before scientific interpretation; charge all failed checks and do not auto-duplicate unknown jobs.')\n],\n'cost_plan':{\n 'estimate_ref':'g0-r0017-available_norm measured wall333.117s/train300.629s and g0-r0018-block_energy_global wall333.176s/train300.766s, compared with local339.552s. Runtime protocol conservative full-unit estimate481.3475877419114s, trial cap1203.3689693547785s, remaining138893.56453990936s at entry.',\n 'all_variants_counted':True,\n 'attribution_reserve':'Submit four full-data cells, all charged, approximately4*481.35=1925.4s planning allowance; hard per-trial cap unchanged, worst admitted four-cap cost4813.5s. No screen, local training, installation or test request. Added fixed reductions have unknown host cost; no speedup claimed. Keep at least12 conservative full units (~5776s) for meaningful attribution and three paired seeds for the selected candidate and closest controls when the host permits, rather than counting parity bridges as repetitions.',\n 'assessment_reserve':'Keep at least10 conservative units (~4814s) for freeze/checks and a host-authorized final assessment suite. No held-out access in propose phase. Selection and source/config/checkpoint identities, closest references, key controls and seeds must be frozen before any closed assessment; withheld results may not reenter open research.',\n 'stop_rule':'Stop at the recorded hard deadline or trial cap, on integrity failure, or when no admissible contrast plus attribution/assessment reserves fits. All preparation, static/scalar diagnostics, agent time, failures and retries consume wall-clock budget. This phase ends with proposal/modules; only the host can train or score. Do not expand the budget or silently retry an execution with unknown state.'\n}}\nconfigs={}\nvariants=[]\nfor name,f,role,detail in [\n ('cubic_ordered','candidate.py','candidate','Replace the redundant fifth match direction with the orthogonal coarse cubic; eligibility and norm match the two replacement controls.'),\n ('cubic_scrambled','coarse_scrambled.py','control','Fixed scrambled-rank cubic residual; same projection bases, gate, norm, contraction and learned capacity. Some sparse block patterns produce collinear directions.'),\n ('cubic_gated_duplicate','coarse_duplicate.py','control','Incumbent fifth multiplied by the exact common new eligibility; isolates support gating from new information.'),\n ('cubic_bridge','coarse_bridge.py','control','Return exact incumbent available_norm fifth after computing all new alternatives. Same-seed parity and cost bridge, not independent replication.')]:\n s=Path(f).read_text();tree=ast.parse(s)\n config=next(ast.literal_eval(n.value) for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets))\n digest=hashlib.sha256(s.encode()).hexdigest()\n note=detail+' Expected unchanged32129765 total/336549 dense parameters, host confirmation required. Static syntax/CONFIG/default/import checks, identical inherited core methods and module allocations, and full-module AST parity modulo CONFIG/mode default passed. Independent scalar FP64 specification:4575 mask/affinity cases;1318 eligible,1095 with noncollinear ordered/scrambled directions; maximum basis dot1.42e-14 and norm2 error4.44e-14. Algebraic witness retains new response0.058121 while old summary coefficient contractions are at most3.61e-16. These specification checks do not execute torch or establish BF16 tensor/gradient correctness or predictive performance. Host forward/backward/masking/gradient-ownership/numerical checks, parameters, measured cost and validation are pending. No training, installations or held-out access performed. SHA256='+digest+'.'\n variants.append(dict(name=name,file=f,role=role,config=config,note=note))\nassess=[]\nfor kid,why,diff in [\n ('unirank-method-unimixer','Card and pinned benchmark forward175-200 inspected. Full flattening and learned tokenization change many factors; local evidence motivates a narrow capacity-fixed coarse-information test first.','A fixed masked cubic projection feeds inherited task adapters, rather than learned flatten-history tokens and UniMixing blocks; original author paper detail unavailable.'),\n ('unirank-method-ssr','Card and primary benchmark line21 inspected. Competitive sparse filtering targets activation selection after pooling, rather than the missing coarse ordinal direction; not adopted.','No sparse filtering, competitive activation or multi-view fusion added.'),\n ('unirank-method-ultrahstu','Card and primary benchmark line39 inspected. Full sequence transduction and attention sparsity would change capacity, information flow and computation together; not adopted for this contrast.','No event-token transduction, hybrid attention or truncation change added.'),\n ('unirank-method-hiformer','Card and primary benchmark line9 inspected. Heterogeneous field/task token interactions remain a distinct alternative but would not isolate the fifth summary information.','No hierarchical field/task tokenization or HiFormer blocks added; inherited task-specific adapters remain fixed.')]:\n assess.append(dict(knowledge_id=kid,decision='considered',rationale=why+' Benchmark description is not original-method full-paper verification or evidence of local effectiveness.',transformed_mechanism='None from this card. Candidate mechanism is the local evidence-derived coarse cubic replacement.',variant_names=[],nearest_work_difference=diff+' Novelty unverified.',falsifier='This local contrast can reject useful cubic replacement but cannot refute the external method.'))\nassess.append(dict(knowledge_id='paper:din',decision='used',rationale='Read archived primary lines271-282. Retain unnormalized learned activation and the inherited intensity-carrying source path; the new contrast is a supplemental ordinal residual, not attention softmax.',transformed_mechanism='Preserve the existing adapted DIN pooling in all cells; replace only the fifth resi